# Composite keys

## When one column isn't enough

- A **primary key made of 2+ columns**, unique only **in combination**

```
order_id | line_no | product_id | qty
  1001   |   1     |   P-77     |  2
  1001   |   2     |   P-88     |  1     order_id + line_no
  1002   |   1     |   P-77     |  5     together = one line
```

## Where they show up

- **Bridge / junction** tables — the pair of FKs *is* the key (`student_id, course_id`)
- **Weak entities** — parent key + a local discriminator
- **Fact tables** — the combination of **dimension FKs** defines the grain

## The catch

- **Wide & awkward to join** — every reference carries *all* the columns
- Warehouses swap in a single narrow **surrogate key**, keep the composite as attributes
